      {
        "fields": {
          "quote": "Number 1, but we have to be aware that users can bring their own LLM so we need to leave that open. I think global configuration is a good place for things like this. ",
          "statement": "A headless LLM call (Haiku by default) classifies a failure as transient or real; which model or command runs is a machine-wide (global) setting so users can bring their own LLM; the hard-coded signature list goes; when the call cannot run there is no retry"
        },
        "handle": "d-llm-classifier",
